# What never reaches a Docker build context.
#
# One image builds from the repository root — services/greenv-measurement-worker, which has to
# carry `measurement/` because it spawns Verge Studio as a process. Without this file the daemon
# is handed the entire working tree: recorded runs, installed dependencies and virtual
# environments included, against the few megabytes of source the image actually COPYs.
#
# It has to live HERE. Docker reads a .dockerignore from the context root, or from
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` beside the named Dockerfile — never from the service directory of
# the image being built, which is why an earlier services/greenv-measurement-worker/.dockerignore
# was silently inert.
#
# The patterns follow .gitignore, for the same reason: the tree a build reads and the tree git
# records are both the source, and neither wants what a tool regenerated.

# Version control, and the agent worktrees — each one is another checkout of this repository, so
# leaving them in sends the whole tree a second time.
.git
.claude/worktrees

# Dependencies and build output. Every image installs from a lockfile instead.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# JVM, Python, Flutter and Terraform working trees.
**/.gradle
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.dart_tool
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfplan

# Recorded runs and session scratch. `measurement/fixtures/` is the one place this repository
# tracks a large artifact on purpose — 12 MB of roadside reconstruction that Verge Studio's tests
# read from the source tree. Nothing inside an image ever opens it.
measurement/fixtures
**/.runs
**/.inspect

# Secrets and machine-local configuration. The runtime environment carries these; a layer that
# baked one in would keep it for the life of the image.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.local.json
